==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|enthral||UK}}
* {{alter|en|inthrall||archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|enthrallen}}, equivalent to {{af|en|en-|thrall}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈθɹɔːl/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-enthrall.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[hold]] [[spellbound]].
#: {{syn|en|bewitch|captivate|charm|enchant|transfix}}
#* {{RQ:Wilde Dorian Gray|chapter=5|passage=Fancy, Jim, to be in love and play Juliet! To have him sitting there! To play for his delight! I am afraid I may frighten the company, frighten or '''enthrall''' them.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1913|chapter=17|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/files/81/81-h/81-h.htm|title=The Return of Tarzan|author=Edgar Rice Burroughs|authorlink=Edgar Rice Burroughs|passage=In the center of the circle of glittering black bodies he leaped and roared and shook his heavy spear in the same mad abandon that '''enthralled''' his fellow savages. The last remnant of his civilization was forgotten—he was a primitive man to the fullest now; reveling in the freedom of the fierce, wild life he loved, gloating in his kingship among these wild blacks.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|rare}} To make [[subservient]].
#: {{syn|en|enslave|subjugate}}
#: {{ant|en|disenthrall}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=XII|passage={{...|Therefore, since he permits / Within himself unworthy powers to reign / Over free reason, God, in judgement just, / Subjects him from without to violent lords; /}} Who oft as undeservedly '''enthrall''' / His outward freedom:  Tyranny must be;}}

